---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import data from '../../../data/generated/ca-5gc-sim.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const href = (value: string) => `${base.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}${value.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;
---
<SiteLayout title="Sandbox documentation" lang="en" description="Sandbox platform architecture, component ownership, reliability benchmarks, and public interface documentation.">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="home-kicker">SANDBOX · PLATFORM DOCUMENTATION</div>
    <h1>Sandbox platform documentation</h1>
    <p>Sandbox composes Agent, tool, environment, experiment-control, and evaluation components into repeatable systems. This site describes the platform architecture and responsibility boundaries, and links to public interfaces and contracts maintained by each component.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a href={href('/en/architecture/system/#real-5gc-workflow')}>Real 5GC workflow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/runbooks/real-5gc/')}>Real 5GC runbook <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/interfaces/real-5gc-evidence/')}>Interfaces and evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>Benchmark design <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Platform overview</h2>
    <p>Sandbox is the product-level composition and governance layer. It is not a simulator and does not take ownership of domain facts held by individual components. It can compose simulated, real, or hybrid environments.</p>
    <div class="reading-list">
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/architecture/system/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">01</span>
        <span><strong>Platform architecture and component boundaries</strong><small>Follow an SBI request through Open5GS / UERANSIM, Fabric, SCP, Agent, and Runtime, including the distinction between R1 and R2-B.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">02</span>
        <span><strong>Benchmark and reliability evaluation</strong><small>Learn the boundaries between evaluation assets, the system under test, frozen tasks, execution attempts, evidence adjudication, and aggregation.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/architecture/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">03</span>
        <span><strong>Documentation sources and governance</strong><small>How components declare public documentation sources, and how this site validates, synchronizes, and publishes snapshots.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Component reference</h2>
    <p>Platform documents describe how components are composed. Each component's owner repository remains authoritative for interface, state, and operation definitions.</p>
    <table class="component-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Plane</th><th>Public reference</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/')}>env-5gc-sim</a></td>
          <td>Environment Plane</td>
          <td><a href={href('/en/api/')}>API</a> · <a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/facts/')}>Facts ({data.counts.facts})</a> · <a href={href('/en/components/ca-5gc-sim/operations/')}>Operations ({data.counts.operations})</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/tool-common/')}>tool-common</a></td>
          <td>Tool Plane</td>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/tool-common/')}>Overview</a> · <a href={href('/en/components/tool-common/subject-identity/')}>Subject Identity</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/sandbox/')}>Sandbox architecture</a></td>
          <td>Platform / Governance</td>
          <td>Detailed architecture, responsibility boundaries, and Benchmark framework</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/ca-benchmarks/')}>Benchmark assets</a></td>
          <td>Evaluation</td>
          <td>Initial 13 Cases, Mode applicability, and evidence semantics</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href={href('/en/components/ca-benchmark-engine/')}>Benchmark Engine</a></td>
          <td>Evaluation</td>
          <td>Task freezing, Attempts, Validity, and result semantics</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="home-footnote">This table lists only currently integrated public references; it is not the complete Sandbox component inventory. Component migrations and repository renames follow the status maintained by each owner repository.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Documentation and implementation status</h2>
    <p>This site owns platform-level explanations, cross-repository navigation, and validated public snapshots. Component owner repositories remain authoritative for implementation, machine contracts, and domain facts. The target architecture is established, while cross-repository migration and consumer acceptance continue in stages; an accepted design does not mean every capability is implemented.</p>
    <p><a href={href('/en/architecture/')}>Read the documentation source and synchronization rules →</a></p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
